Base Search {{VERSION}}
==================

Package: {{PLATFORM}} / {{ARCH}}

Start
-----
{{START_INSTRUCTIONS}}

Base Search starts the local launcher by default. The launcher starts the
embedded browser workspace, waits until it is healthy, and opens it in the
default browser. The previous native workspace remains available as an
explicit fallback with the --legacy-desktop option.

Data
----
This public package contains no database, spreadsheet, import, export, or test
data. The included data directory is intentionally empty. Base Search creates
base_search.db on first use. It prefers the writable package data directory
and falls back to the current user's home directory when the package location
is read-only.

Analytics engines
-----------------
This production package contains SQLite + FTS5 search and DuckDB OLAP. The
server capability can be checked at /api/v2/engines while Base Search is
running. A DuckDB projection is created only when the user requests an OLAP
build; it is not bundled in this package.

Command line
------------
{{CLI_INSTRUCTIONS}}

Security
--------
Personal mode listens only on 127.0.0.1. LAN mode is an explicit trusted-network
option and requires an owner account. Do not expose the unencrypted local LAN
server directly to the public internet.

